problem_statement:
Add a dedicated exception for bad input:

- in `app/errors.py`, define `class ValidationError(AppError)`;
- `app/validators.py` currently raises ValueError in `check_age(age)` for ages outside 0-150; it must raise ValidationError instead;
- `app/api.py` has `handle(age)` that returns (200, "ok") for good input; it must return (400, <the error message>) when `check_age` raises ValidationError. Other exceptions must still propagate.
